---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Who writes Budget Home Fixes and how our cost estimates are put together."
>
  <h1>About Budget Home Fixes</h1>
  <p>
    Budget Home Fixes publishes practical cost breakdowns and comparisons for home upgrades,
    aimed at renters and anyone working with a tight budget. We focus on one question for every
    article: how much will this actually cost, and what's the cheaper alternative?
  </p>
  <h2>How we put together our numbers</h2>
  <p>
    Our cost estimates are built from publicly available pricing at major retailers, manufacturer
    coverage specs (e.g. paint coverage per gallon), and published industry rate guides for
    professional labor. Every article lists its assumptions (room size, number of coats, etc.)
    so you can adjust the numbers to your own situation — our calculators let you plug in your
    exact measurements instead of relying on a generic average.
  </p>
  <p>
    Prices change often and vary by region. We review and update articles periodically, but
    always treat our numbers as a starting estimate, not a quote.
  </p>
  <h2>Spot an error?</h2>
  <p>
    If a price or figure looks off, let us know at <a href="mailto:hello@thebudgethomefixes.com">hello@thebudgethomefixes.com</a> and we'll correct it.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
